Entity: (Primary Balancing Segment) ensures that all journals balance for use in trial balance reporting. The Entity segment will represent the legal entity. The values in the Entity segment will be linked to legal entities, to ensure correct accounting by legal entity. Cost Centre: facilitates grouping of natural accounts by functional cost types, accommodating tracking of specific business expenses across natural accounts). Account: (Nominal Account) determines the account type (asset, liability, expense, revenue, or equity)
Trading Partner: allows [Anonymized Customer] to track inter-legal entity transactions and make full use of the standard intercompany processes in Oracle Cloud. Business Spare: a spare segment which can be used in the future, set to default value (all zeros) until then. Future Spare1: a spare segment which can be used in the future, set to default value (all zeros) until then. Segment Values will be a fixed length and the Segment separator will be ‘.’
Dynamic insertion will be enabled. Dynamic insertion allows the creation of account code combinations automatically the first time your users enter that new account combination, if the new combination satisfies any existing cross-validation rules. The Enterprise Structures configuration workbook contain a full description of the values and rules associated with the COA Design. The Chart of Accounts for [Anonymized Customer] will be mastered in the Enterprise Data Management (EDM) Cloud Service. This will enable:
Governance of the Chart of Accounts:
Controlling the addition of new child and parent accounts;
Controlling the amendment and end-dating of existing accounts;
Maintenance of Cross-validation rules;
Control of reporting hierarchies. Mapping between the [Anonymized] Global COA and the Legacy COA
The Chart of accounts within ERP Cloud will be updated from Enterprise Data Management Cloud Service using the standard adaptors in EPM data management configuration.
